cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, model, or its derived results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Poverty Point Costly Signaling: Agent-Based Model and Analysis Code"
abstract: >-
  Agent-based model, analytical equilibrium analyses, GIS analyses, and figure-generation
  pipeline for an investigation of Poverty Point (ca. 1700-1100 BCE) as an adaptive
  costly-signaling system among Late Archaic mobile hunter-gatherers in the Lower
  Mississippi Valley. Implements coupled signaling rules under environmental uncertainty,
  multi-drainage shortfall buffering, and a Bayesian posterior predictive check against
  monument and exotic-goods records.
